\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces  Learning-rate and LoRA ablation at 1000/20 (stealth-95, 5 seeds, benign-calibrated threshold). Unfrozen baseline and LR/LoRA rows use 5 seeds; frozen row uses 10 seeds (B$=$C$=$D, identical; see Table~\ref {tab:scaling}). \textbf  {Key findings}: (1)~$10^{-5}$ partially mitigates degradation for C but not B or D. (2)~$10^{-6}$ underfits across all conditions. (3)~LoRA (rank$=$8) underperforms full freezing, suggesting low-rank adapters lack capacity for this task. (4)~Full encoder freezing remains the most effective mitigation. }}{23}{table.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
